# Practice presentation (forward momentum)

**Steve rule:** Briefing + Play **HPI tab** = what the learner sees **before** workup. Never dump diagnosis, fundoscopy results, LP opening pressure, or treatment plan there.

## Two HPI fields (do not conflate)

| Field | Purpose | Shown in practice HPI tab? |
|-------|---------|----------------------------|
| **`practice_hpi`** | Spoiler-free presentation (symptoms, PMH cues only) | **Yes** — preferred |
| **`hpi_narrative`** | DeepSeek answer-key / teach chart (full workup + treatment) | **No** — teach, notes, chat context only |

Add `practice_hpi` to `preparedCases.json` (and `game/data/cases/case_N.json` when syncing bank) for any case whose `hpi_narrative` contains spoilers.

**Batch audit (dev):** `node scripts/audit-learner-spoilers.mjs` → `docs/learner-spoiler-audit.md`  
**Batch fix:** `node scripts/fix-learner-presentation.mjs --write --force` (rebuilds all `practice_hpi` from answer-key)

## HPI bans (learner-facing)

Never in **`practice_hpi`**, `narrative.*.hpi`, or briefing/play HPI:

- Diagnosis names or classification (SJS, TEN, DKA, IIH, …)
- Exam findings that belong after a dedicated order (Nikolsky, BSA %, biopsy read)
- Treatment plan (stop drug, admit ICU, consults)
- Teaching pivots ("classic 1–8 week window", "offending agent", "new diagnosis — stop now")
- Pathophysiology or "consistent with …"

**OK in HPI:** symptoms, timeline, patient-reported mouth/eye pain, med names and start dates as facts (no causality lecture).

## Physical exam bans (initial `exam` array — Exam tab before orders)

Exam text must be **objective bedside documentation** — what you see/hear/feel, not what you conclude.

| Ban | Use instead |
|-----|-------------|
| "no acute surgical abdomen" | "Soft, non-distended, non-tender" |
| "SJS not TEN" / "(SJS)" / "<10% BSA" labels | Omit classification; state findings only |
| Nikolsky, BSA detachment, full mucosal survey | Defer to **full skin exam** stack result |
| Negative differentials ("not TEN", "not SSSS") | Omit — learner rules those out |

**Order results** (labs, biopsy, dedicated skin exam): report **raw values and histology** without diagnosis labels unless the order is literally "pathology read with diagnosis" (prefer neutral histology text).

**Attendant canon** in `docs/cases/*.md` may keep teaching inferences in a separate **Attendant / answer-key** section — never copy that block into `practice_hpi` or initial `exam`.


| Function | Must use |
|----------|----------|
| `getBriefingHpi()` | `presentationHistory` / `historyText` / `practice_hpi` — **never** `hpi_narrative` first |
| `applySessionToCase()` | Keep `historyText` on practice source — **do not** overwrite with `hpi_narrative` |
| `CaseContextPanel` HPI body | `hpiText` prop / `historyText` — **never** `caseData.hpi_narrative` for display |
| `getBriefingNotes()` | Full chart (diagnosis, treatment) — **Notes tab only** |

## CCS shared titles

Cases that share a presentation title (e.g. many **Headache** cases) may get generic CCS `historyText`. Case-specific DeepSeek cases still need their own **`practice_hpi`** when the diagnosis differs (e.g. case 140 IIH).

## Read case control

- **Read case** = gold pill top-right (`pack-tag--read`), replaces Immersa brand tag in case chrome.
- Not a second row under tab icons. Briefing with `hideHeader` → read pill on tab row.
